## ⚠️ Scope — screen creation + live prototyping ONLY

This context **consumes the published {{SYSTEM_NAME}} design system** to:
1. **Build / recreate consumer screens** by composing {{SYSTEM_NAME}} components in the CONSUMER Figma
   file (`{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}`), plus the UX definition that precedes pixels (flows, IA,
   state matrices, interaction + a11y specs, functional microcopy).
2. **Build live coded prototypes** (React/Vite, instrumented for usability testing) under
   `prototypes/` — the **required usability-validation gate**: every flow is usability-tested as a
   coded prototype *before* it goes live or is handed to the product team + engineers. This proves
   the design *works for users*, which the Figma fidelity gates cannot. A failed test routes back to
   `ux-designer` / `ui-designer`, not forward.

**Out of scope — the SEPARATE `{{DS_REPO}}` owns these:** the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} design system
itself — tokens, styles, components, variants, bindings, the manifest, publish, drift, and
the spiels mechanism. That context **publishes** {{SYSTEM_NAME}} + updates its `skills/`+`manifest/`;
**this** context consumes the published library. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found while building a screen
routes **back to that context** as a tokenization / component request — never hand-build a
{{SYSTEM_NAME}} equivalent here (that is the drift boundary).

> **`ds_mode` note ({{DS_MODE}}):** in **consume** mode the `library_key` below points at an already
> *published* {{SYSTEM_NAME}} system and the read-only mirrors are live snapshots of it. In **build** mode the
> sibling DS context is still authoring {{SYSTEM_NAME}}; the `library_key` + mirrors fill in **after the DS
> context's first publish**, and until then component keys/versions may be placeholders. Either way,
> this context never authors {{SYSTEM_NAME}} source — it consumes whatever the DS context has published.

**Hard rules:**
- **Never author or publish {{SYSTEM_NAME}} source** (`{{DS_FIGMA_KEY}}`) here — read-only reference.
- **Compose, don't reinvent.** About to hand-build a row / amount field / inner-screen header /
  dialog → STOP, use the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} component, or file a gap to the DS context.
- Screen Figma writes use `use_figma` (requires the Figma Desktop Bridge). Coded prototypes are
  ordinary local dev (Vite) — that's expected and in-scope here (unlike the DS context).

