## Critical rules (always)

1. **Consume, never author {{SYSTEM_NAME}} source** — tokens/components/variants are owned + published by the DS context. File a gap; don't hand-build a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} equivalent (that's drift).
2. **`use_figma` requires font loading** — load all {{FONTS}} weights before any text op (screen Figma writes).
3. **Render-verify after every visual change** — screenshot to confirm; no "looks fine" without one.
4. **Three gates before handoff** — (a) the design-review lens (zero blockers) + (b) the Gotcha #27 binding audit (zero unbound on NEW frames), both in Figma, THEN (c) the **usability-validation gate**: usability-test the flow as a coded prototype (task success / time-on-task / SEQ + heatmaps) before it goes live or reaches product + engineering.
5. **Honest scope notes always** — flag any unavoidable hardcoded stopgap as a DS gap routed to the DS context.
6. **Prototypes carry no secrets in git** — `.env` (Clarity/PostHog/auth) + `.vercel` stay gitignored.
7. **Plan Mode before consumer-file builds** — a screen build is a write; plan in `yaml` and approve before mutating the consumer file.
8. **Verify consumption after a DS publish** — a publish isn't "landed" here until consumer screens actually show it. Run `rebind` (interactive) or `consumer-migrator` (sweep) to swap stale instances onto the fresh main, rebind overrides, and re-audit. Instances cache old layout until swapped (Gotcha #20).

